course: dictionary
lesson: 6327
title: Words for machines and vehicles
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A motorbike is a heavy vehicle with two wheels and an engine. It is like a bicycle with a motor. The word is made of two parts: motor (the engine) and bike (a two-wheeled vehicle). If you know both parts, you can often work out a new word.
explain: «A motorbike leans into bends to turn; motorbikes are fast and hard to see, so look twice before crossing.» The clues here are leans, bends and fast. Leaning means tilting sideways, so a rider leans to turn, just as a bicycle rider does. Fast and hard to see tell you why we must take care.
explain: Some words mean the same thing. A motorbike is also called a motorcycle, so both words name the same vehicle. When you meet a new word, check the words around it. Often the writer is giving you a clue to its meaning.
fact: A motorbike is a heavy two-wheeled vehicle with an engine.
fact: Motorbike and motorcycle mean the same thing.
fact: «Motorbikes are fast and hard to see», so drivers and walkers must look carefully before crossing.
fact: Riders must wear helmets to keep their heads safe.
fact: In maths, speed is distance ÷ time, and distance = speed × time.
exercise: «A motorbike leans into bends to turn.» What is a motorbike? | A tall building with many windows | A small boat with a sail | A kind of bird that flies very fast | *A heavy two-wheeled vehicle with an engine
exercise: Another name for a motorbike is a what? | lorry | *motorcycle | tractor
exercise: «Motorbikes are fast and hard to see, so look twice before crossing.» Why should you look twice? | Motorbikes are slow and very quiet | *Motorbikes are fast and hard to see | Motorbikes always stop at crossings | Motorbikes have no wheels
test: A motorbike has how many wheels? | Three | Four | One | *Two
test: Riders of a motorbike must wear what to keep their head safe? | A scarf | *A helmet | A raincoat
exam: A motorbike travels 60 km in 1 hour. What is its speed? | 61 km per hour | 1 km per hour | 60 hours | *60 km per hour
